  "live_records": {
    "q-33092": {
      "dom_id": "step-q33092",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "${(\\frac{p}{2}+\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}=$",
      "worked_solution": "We will use the following formula:\n\n$$\n(a+b)^{2}={a}^{2}+2ab+{b}^{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=\\frac{p}{2}$ and $b=\\frac{3}{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{p}{2}+\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & = \\\\ {(\\frac{p}{2})}^{2}+2(\\frac{p}{2})(\\frac{3}{2})+{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & = \\\\ \\frac{{p}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{3}{2}p+\\frac{9}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
