      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "${(3{m}^{4}+5n)}^{2}=${{field-1}}${m}^{8}\\,\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${m}^{4}n\\,\\,+$\n{{field-3}}${n}^{2}$",
      "worked_solution": "We will use the following formula:\n\n$$\n(a+b)^{2}={a}^{2}+2ab+{b}^{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=3{m}^{4}$ and $b=5n,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(3{m}^{4}+5n)}^{2} & = \\\\ {(3{m}^{4})}^{2}+2(3{m}^{4})(5n)+{(5n)}^{2} & = \\\\ 9{m}^{8}+30{m}^{4}n+25{n}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
