      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "${(2{x}^{2}+3)}^{2}\\,\\,=\\,\\,${{field-1}}${x}^{4}\\,\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,\\,+9$",
      "worked_solution": "We will use the following formula:\n\n$$\n(a+b)^{2}={a}^{2}+2ab+{b}^{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=2{x}^{2}$ and $b=3,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(2{x}^{2}+3)}^{2} & = \\\\ {(2{x}^{2})}^{2}+2(2{x}^{2})(3)+{3}^{2} & = \\\\ 4{x}^{4}+12{x}^{2}+9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
