      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "${(7{m}^{2}+4n)}^{2}=${{field-1}}${m}^{4}\\,\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${m}^{2}n\\,\\,+$\n{{field-3}}${n}^{2}$",
      "worked_solution": "We will use the following formula:\n\n$$\n(a+b)^{2}={a}^{2}+2ab+{b}^{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=7{m}^{2}$ and $b=4n,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(7{m}^{2}+4n)}^{2} & = \\\\ {(7{m}^{2})}^{2}+2(7{m}^{2})(4n)+(4n)^{2} & = \\\\ 49{m}^{4}+56{m}^{2}n+16{n}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
