      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "${({y}^{3}-2)}^{2}=$",
      "worked_solution": "We will use the following formula:\n\n$$\n(a-b)^{2}={a}^{2}-2ab+{b}^{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a={y}^{3}$ and $b=2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({y}^{3}-2)^{2} & = \\\\ {({y}^{3})}^{2}-2({y}^{3})(2)+{2}^{2} & = \\\\ {y}^{6}-4{y}^{3}+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
